<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/035P">Remark <span data-tag="035P">5.3.1.13</span>.</a> We will be primarily interested in the special case of Notation <a data-tag="02T1" href="/tag/02T1">5.3.1.10</a> where $U': \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}' \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a left fibration of simplicial sets. In this case, an object $F \in \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}', \operatorname{\mathcal{E}})$ belongs to the full subcategory $\operatorname{Fun}^{\operatorname{CCart}}_{/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}', \operatorname{\mathcal{E}})$ if and only if it carries <em>every</em> edge of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'$ to a $U$-cocartesian edge of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ (Proposition <a data-tag="01UM" href="/tag/01UM">5.1.4.15</a>). </p>
